4 0 obj
<< /Length 572 >>
stream
BT /F2 16 Tf 60 760 Td (2. Background and Problem Statement) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 726 Td (PostgreSQL read traffic grew 300% over the last quarter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 708 Td (Peak-hour CPU utilization on the primary replica reached 85% and P95) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 690 Td (query latency exceeded 1.2 seconds, violating our 200ms target.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 672 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 654 Td (Root cause: repeated execution of hot read queries that change rarely,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 636 Td (including product catalog lookups and user session joins.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
5 0 obj
<< /Length 1030 >>
stream
BT /F2 16 Tf 60 760 Td (3. Proposed Solution: Redis Caching Layer) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 726 Td (Section 3.2 - Data Flow) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 708 Td (A Redis cache sits between application servers and PostgreSQL.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 690 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 672 Td (Read path:  App Server -> Redis -> \(on miss\) -> PostgreSQL,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 654 Td (            then populate Redis with TTL of 300 seconds \(5 minutes\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 636 Td (Write path: App Server -> PostgreSQL first, then synchronously) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 618 Td (            invalidate and refresh the matching Redis key) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 600 Td (            \(write-through pattern\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 582 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 564 Td (Expected impact: about 60% of read queries served from Redis,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 546 Td (reducing database load proportionally. See Figure 7-1, appendix page 7) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 528 Td (for the complete annotated data-flow diagram discussed in the meeting.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
6 0 obj
<< /Length 540 >>
stream
BT /F2 16 Tf 60 760 Td (4. Operational Notes) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 726 Td (QPS target: 10,000 sustained. SLA: 99.9% availability.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 708 Td (If Redis is unavailable all traffic falls back to PostgreSQL;) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 690 Td (Redis sits on the performance critical path, not the availability path.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 672 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 654 Td (Appendix reference: Figure 7-1 on page 7 mirrors the slide shown at) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 60 636 Td (minute 00:40 in the recorded review session.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
